99
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:08,340
Chicago was the railroad, grain, and
communications hub of the American

100
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:09,380
Midwest.

101
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:13,780
Even while blocks were still burning,
operators sent urgent dispatches racing

102
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:15,540
to New York, Washington, and London.

103
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:19,960
Relief trains loaded with food, lumber,
and millions of dollars in donations

104
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,840
rolled toward Chicago within days.

105
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:26,260
Up in Peshtigo, every single telegraph
pole had burned to the ground.

106
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:30,840
Word of the Wisconsin catastrophe had
to travel slowly by survivor wagon and

107
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:35,100
boat down to Green Bay, and it took days
before Governor Lucius Fairchild even

108
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:39,000
learned the scale of the loss, by which
time Wisconsin's relief supplies were

109
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,580
